# modifyOtherKeys waits while the kitty keyboard protocol's flags are not
# 0: XTMODKEYS still sets its level and XTQMODKEYS still reports it, but
# the protocol decides the keys' bytes until a pop puts 0 in force again.
# spec: kitty's Comprehensive keyboard handling in terminals: Progressive enhancement; ctlseqs, XTMODKEYS and modifyOtherKeys; ADR-1005, D6
# covers: input.kitty-keyboard
size 20 2
send "\e[>4;2m"
key 1 mods=ctrl
send "\e[>1u"
key 1 mods=ctrl
send "\e[?4m"
send "\e[>4;1m"
key a mods=alt
send "\e[<u"
key a mods=alt
key Escape
